From 174eacc96169da8e06073ef8cb75ee9ae1d50321 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:55:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: move Linux jobs from self-hosted tfgar lanes to
 Blacksmith; repo is example-org/hermes [daveey]

The repo moved to the example-org org (formerly Example-AI), whose
billing runs GitHub-hosted and Blacksmith jobs. The personal account's
hosted jobs were refused for billing, so CI ran on one ephemeral EC2 VM
per job: about 10k launches on 2026-11-03, with a median queue wait of
53 s for a 19 s ci-fast job.

- runs-on: ci-fast and hermes-hub-poll go to blacksmith-2vcpu,
  hermes-hub and hermes-hub-ci to 4vcpu, and docker-ci, tfgar-tests and
  ci-bwrap to 8vcpu. The macOS hermes-state lane and tfgar-probe stay.
- scripts/fork-ci-runner.sh re-points upstream and retired self-hosted
  labels to these sizes and stays idempotent.
- bubblewrap: e2e-upgrade already lifts the userns restriction itself.
  plugin-catalog's pinned-source-validate gets one named setup step
  ahead of its fail-closed proof.
- Repository identity checks name example-org/hermes, so the
  fork-only gates keep their meaning after the transfer.
- The routing tests encode the new lanes.
